  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1127 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nGoing into the long term, upper level high pressure is expected \nto dominate once again with very little prospects for \nprecipitation. This means the return of heat headlines and \nmonsoonal moisture staying primarily west of the CWA. Cimarron may\nsee some chances for showers or thunderstorms to creep in from \nthe north to northwest before fizzling out, but the rest of the \ncombined Panhandles are looking to primarily stay high and dry. \nCurrently there are no signs of Td's in the 60s, therefore, not \nlooking to be worried about that warm souping air seen in the gulf\nof the Midwest. But more typical Panhandle dry air, even for the \neastern stack of counties.",
